window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>A Coven Lost: Book 2 of the Triquetra Series (A Supernatural historical fiction set in the backdrop of Scottish Witch Trials)</p> <p>Before the flames, there was betrayal.</p> <p>Scotland, 1618. The Triquetra Coven stands at the height of its power—respected, feared, and hidden in plain sight along the windswept coast of Irvine. At its helm, Margaret Barclay, a fierce and visionary leader, pushes her members to master their gifts and protect their legacy. But when she is slighted by her husband’s family, Margaret’s thirst for justice awakens a storm that could destroy everything she has built.</p> <p>Emily Swan, a young initiate destined to inherit the mantle of leadership, sees a different path forward—one of peace, compassion, and openness. Alongside Thomas Stewart, her betrothed and fellow coven member, Emily dreams of a future where the coven can live without fear. But their ideals are threatened as the old guard seeks vengeance, drawing unwanted eyes to their sacred circle.</p> <p>As the Church tightens its grip and betrayals rise from within, the coven faces its greatest threat yet. Accusations of witchcraft begin to swirl. Torture extracts confessions. Fires are lit.</p> <p>Inspired by the real witch trials of 17th-century Scotland, <i>A Coven Lost</i> is a haunting and powerful tale of love, loyalty, and sacrifice. It is the story of a coven betrayed—not by their magic, but by those they trusted most.</p> <p>If you have listened to and enjoyed <i>The Familiars</i> by Stacey Hall, <i>The Witch’s Daughter</i> by Paula Brackston, <i>The Heretic’s Daughter</i> by Kathleen Kent, <i>Time-Slip, Legacy, and Female Power, The Daughters of the Witching Hill</i> by Mary Sharratt or <i>The Once and Future Witches</i> by Alix E. Harrow, then thou will enjoy this supernatural historical fiction.</p>"; 
